# 2026-08-12 — wholesale 301 to councilof.ai REMOVED (Kimi, AZ audit).
# The 2026-08-10 wildcard was a stopgap for the Vercel-1034 apex outage ("csoai is
# borken, just redirect it"). www.csoai.org is healthy again (verified serving packs),
# and the wildcard was an SEO/AEO hazard: it dropped deep paths (csoai.org/<pack> ->
# councilof.ai homepage), and councilof.ai answers every path with a meta-refresh
# shell — so 456 pack URLs were funnelling into an unrelated shell page.
# Restore directive with one commit if the consolidation is still wanted — but the
# correct form is /* -> https://councilof.ai/:splat 301 (path-preserving), and only
# once the packs actually exist on councilof.ai.
# Apex (csoai.org bare) still needs the Namecheap ALIAS record (Nick's manual item);
# the 1034 never reaches Pages, so no _redirects rule can fix apex from here.

# /about used to 301 to /index.html (my pre-C3 audit fix). Now /about has its own
# page. Remove the rule so the real /about.html serves.
# (NOTE: clean-trailing-slash is handled by the default Pages 308 to drop the .html)

# /arena and /gspc-arena must resolve to the real 12-greenfields page.
# Without these, Cloudflare Pages serves index.html for the bare path, which
# is the "4-axis GSPC stub hydration crash" observed 2026-08-01.
# The arena-hub page itself is fully static HTML — no JS to hydrate — so a
# correct route + the file = no crash.

# /gate is the refusal-gate demo page; Cloudflare Pages default clean-trailing-slash
# handles /gate/ automatically.
/gate        /gate.html       301
/gate/       /gate.html       301

# /prv and /gspc-prv resolve to the provenance axis page.
# gspc-prv.html is a REAL file. Cloudflare's clean URLs serve it at /gspc-prv
# and /prv natively (same as /master and /provbench). No _redirect rule is
# needed — and the previous 301-to-.html rule created an infinite loop
# (301 → .html → 308 back → 301). Removed 2026-08-08.

